B.aBa=new A.bI("Short version: CrispChess collects nothing about you.\n\nThis app does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data, and has no analytics, no tracking, no advertising, and no account system. All chess computation runs locally on your device.\n\nThe app does make network requests for functional purposes: downloading engine files (Lc0, Stockfish, Lynx) and neural network weights on first use of those engines, and querying a public opening-book/tablebase service from the Opening Explorer. These requests go to the engines' hosting servers (e.g. GitHub Releases) and public chess APIs, and \u2014 like any network request \u2014 expose your IP address to those servers as an unavoidable part of how the internet works. CrispChess itself does not attach any personal data to these requests, and downloaded engine files are cached locally so this only happens once per engine.\n\nThe unfinished game (board position and move history) is saved locally after each move so you can resume it after restarting.\n\nStored on your device, and nowhere else: your settings, engine profiles, game history and Engine Lab benchmark results. A benchmark document records the engines' names and versions, a fingerprint of each executable (a SHA-256 hash, or its size and modification time when hashing is unavailable), the options applied and the games played, plus app/benchmark versions, platform, coarse host summary and environment notes. It does not contain the engine binary's file path, and it is never uploaded. Exports (PGN, CSV, JSON, Markdown) are produced only when you ask for one, and go nowhere until you send them yourself.\n\nThe web version (crispchess.vercel.app) is a static site. Vercel may log standard HTTP access logs (IP, user agent). CrispChess itself sends no personal data to any server.\n\nIf we ever add features that involve storing or transmitting personal data, this policy will be updated and any new data collection will be opt-in.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
